 About Faculty of Allied and Healthcare Sciences 










 The Faculty of Allied and Healthcare Sciences is dedicated to preparing skilled healthcare professionals who support the delivery of quality patient care. Allied Health professionals are trained to provide essential dia
gnostic, therapeutic, rehabilitative, and emergency healthcare services. 


 The faculty aims to develop competent, compassionate, and ethically responsible healthcare personnel capable of meeting the evolving needs of society and the healthcare system. 






 History of the Faculty 


 Founding Authorization: The Government of Uttar Pradesh, through the Uttar Pradesh State Medical Faculty, granted permission to King George’s Medical University (KGMU) to start twelve Allied and Healthcare (Paramedical)
 Diploma Courses vide Letter No. 9573/14 dated 30 October 2014. 



 Inaugural Batch: The first batch of Allied and Healthcare (Paramedical) students was admitted in 2015. An organized administrative structure was established with designated Nodal Officers, Academic In-charges, and Clini
cal Coordinators for each programme. The faculty was initially allotted space in the Kalam Centre. 



 Program Expansion (2017–2019): The Diploma in Blood Transfusion Technician programme was introduced. 



 Program Expansion (2021–2022): The Diploma in Anaesthesia and Critical Care Technician programme was introduced. 



 Current Standing: At present, the faculty offers 14 diploma programmes supported by a robust academic and administrative framework, including Nodal Officers, teaching faculty, and technical staff dedicated to quality ed
ucation and training. 



 Administrative Support: The Dean’s Office is supported by adequate administrative personnel to ensure the smooth functioning of academic and operational activities. 







 New Undergraduate Programmes (Academic Session 2025–26) 

 From the academic session 2025–26, the faculty has introduced three new self-financed undergraduate programmes: 





 S.N. 
 Programme Name 
 Seats / Year 
 Total Duration 
 Structure 




 1 
 Bachelor of Physiotherapy (BPT) 
 10 
 4½ Years 
 4 years academic study + 6 months internship 


 2 
 Bachelor in Medical Laboratory Science (BMLS) 
 20 
 4 Years 
 3½ years academic study + 6 months internship 


 3 
 Bachelor of Optometry (B. Optom.) 
 10 
 4 Years 
 3 years academic study + 1 year internship 








 Mission & Vision 

 MISSION 


 To produce skilled, competent, and compassionate allied health professionals who serve as the first point of healthcare contact and contribute effectively to patient care through professional excellence, ethical practic
e, and strong interpersonal skills. 



 VISION 


 To be a premier institution in allied and healthcare education, imparting competency-based training and fostering excellence in healthcare practice in accordance with contemporary national and global standards. 







 Core Values 


 Our foundational principles guide our academic environment, research initiatives, and professional conduct: 



 Excellence & Innovation: Excellence in education, innovation, and research. 
 Leadership: Leadership, mentorship, and teamwork. 
 Development: Effective communication and lifelong learning. 
 Patient Focus: Patient-centred care and community engagement. 
 Integrity: Ethics, integrity, and professionalism. 
 Well-being: Promotion of comprehensive healthcare and public well-being. 



 The faculty is committed to producing highly trained allied and healthcare professionals with strong moral and ethical values who contribute significantly to healthcare delivery systems and serve as frontline healthcare
 providers whenever required.

